Provide for a buyout cap not exceeding the practitioner’s annual salary and wages at the time of termination;

Buyout Requirement Clarified The covenant must allow for a buyout in an amount not greater than the physician’s total annual salary and wages at the time of termination. This law replaces previous vague language, allowing for an arbitrator’s or court’s determination of what constitutes a “reasonable price.”

With SB 1318, Texas joins a growing number of states refining non-compete rules in healthcare, emphasizing geographic and temporal limits, standardized buyouts, and transparency.
